  // ---- 10 CHROMA
  "Research · 台大碩士研究 · GrAPL @ IPDPS 2026": "Research · NTU Master's Research · GrAPL @ IPDPS 2026",
  "CHROMA：高品質圖著色搬上多 GPU": "CHROMA: High-Quality Graph Coloring on GPUs",
  "高品質的平行圖著色跑得慢、快的方法品質差；CHROMA 把 smallest-last 的 priority allocation 平行化到 GPU": "Quality coloring is slow and fast coloring is poor; CHROMA parallelizes smallest-last priority allocation on GPUs",
  "邊界先上色 · ghost vertices": "boundary first · ghost verts",
  "× 1–8 張（多 GPU 走 RGP）": "× 1–8 GPUs (multi-GPU via RGP)",
  "迴圈掃描效率": "loop scans",
  "θ 粒度可調": "tunable θ",
  "最小度數校正": "min-degree",
  "沿用 ECL-GC kernel": "reuses the ECL-GC kernel",
  "JP 上色示意 · 每一輪平行": "JP coloring · per round",
  "優先的鄰居都上完色 → 選最小可用色": "priority neighbors first → smallest free color",
  "幾何平均加速，顏色數不變": "geomean speedup, same color count",
  "對 192 執行緒 CPU 版本": "vs. the 192-thread CPU version",
  "uk-2002：2 GPU 對 1 GPU": "uk-2002: 2 GPUs vs. 1 GPU",
  "個真實圖 · 最大 5,091 萬頂點": "real-world graphs · up to 50.91M vertices",
  "paperCHROMA: High-Quality Robust Graph Coloring on GPUs · GrAPL @ IPDPS 2026 · 已開源於 GitHub": "<span class=\"tag c\">paper</span>CHROMA: High-Quality Robust Graph Coloring on GPUs · GrAPL @ IPDPS 2026 · open source on GitHub",
  "再來是碩士研究 CHROMA，多 GPU 的圖著色框架，發表在 IPDPS 2026 的 GrAPL workshop。": "Next is my master's research, <strong>CHROMA</strong>, a multi-GPU graph coloring framework published at the <strong>GrAPL workshop at IPDPS 2026</strong>.",
  "背景是：品質好的平行圖著色跑得慢，快的方法上色品質又差。品質好的 smallest-last 排序是循序的，priority allocation 在 CPU 上可以比上色本身慢 100 倍。": "The background: high-quality parallel graph coloring is slow, and the fast methods produce poor colorings. The high-quality smallest-last ordering is sequential, and <strong>on a CPU, priority allocation can be 100× slower than the coloring itself</strong>.",
  "左邊是架構：每張 GPU 先做 priority allocation，我們的 cuSL 把它平行化，再加三個優化：ELS 提高掃描效率、EGC 用 θ 控制每輪的粒度、SDC 校正最小度數保住品質；上色沿用 ECL-GC 的 kernel。多 GPU 時用 RGP 切圖，邊界先上色、子圖帶 ghost vertex。": "On the left is the architecture. Each GPU first runs priority allocation, which our cuSL parallelizes, with three optimizations: ELS improves scan efficiency, EGC uses θ to control the granularity of each round, and SDC corrects the minimum degree to preserve quality. Coloring reuses the ECL-GC kernel. With multiple GPUs, RGP partitions the graph, boundaries are colored first, and each subgraph carries ghost vertices.",
  "右邊是 JP 上色的過程：比自己優先的鄰居都上完色，就挑最小的可用顏色；同一輪可以很多點一起上色，所以適合 GPU。": "On the right is the JP coloring process: once all higher-priority neighbors are colored, a vertex takes the smallest available color. <strong>Many vertices can be colored in the same round</strong>, which is why it suits GPUs.",
  "結果在單張 RTX 4090 上，顏色數不變、幾何平均快 7 倍；比 192 執行緒的 CPU 版快 17 倍。": "On a single RTX 4090 it is <strong>7× faster in geometric mean with the same number of colors</strong>, and 17× faster than the 192-thread CPU version.",
  "CHROMA 的程式基本上都是我寫的：GPU 上的 priority allocation、多 GPU 的 RGP 模組和 CPU baseline。這跟硬體設計的思路很像：找出循序的瓶頸、拆成能平行的結構、再處理同步。": "I wrote basically all of CHROMA's code: <strong>the GPU priority allocation, the multi-GPU RGP module and the CPU baseline</strong>. It's close to how hardware design works: find the sequential bottleneck, break it into a parallel structure, then handle synchronization.",
  "（動畫：P 暫停、逗號／句號一次前進一輪）": "(Animation: P pauses; comma / period move one round at a time.)",
  "（被問到履歷上的 14× 時）那是只開 ELS 的最快設定，顏色數會多三成多；顏色數不變的是 7.14 倍，所以簡報用這個數字。": "(If asked about the 14× on my résumé) That's the fastest setting with only ELS enabled, and it uses over 30% more colors. <strong>With the color count unchanged it's 7.14×</strong>, so that's the number on the slide.",
  "專案就介紹到這裡，接著快速看一下其他作品。": "That's it for projects. Next, a quick look at other work.",
